@startuml uml-sequence-job-execution
title Job execution under an existing agreement — UML sequence diagram

participant "Train Handler" as th
participant "Gateway" as gw
participant "Orchestrator" as orch
participant "PDP" as pdp
participant "Adapter" as adapter
participant "Data source" as ds

alt push dispatch
  th -> gw: POST job (payload + agreement ref)
else poll dispatch — restricted networks
  gw -> th: GET pending jobs
  th --> gw: job (payload + agreement ref)
end

gw -> gw: PEP 1: authn · validate
gw -> orch: enqueue(job)
orch -> pdp: PEP 2: evaluate (agreement · station policy)
pdp --> orch: permit
orch -> adapter: execute(payload)
adapter -> ds: query / run container
ds --> adapter: data / result
adapter --> orch: result
orch -> pdp: PEP 3: result & obligation check
pdp --> orch: permit (+ duties)
orch --> th: artifacts + status

note over th, ds
  Post-execution obligations (e.g. delete results after N days,
  usage reporting) are scheduled by the orchestrator. Every step
  emits an audit event linked to the agreement.
end note
@enduml
